  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The Provençal market on Place des Lices, in the heart of Saint-Tropez, takes place every Tuesday and Saturday morning, from 8am to 1pm, all year round. You'll find food, textiles, decor, crafts and souvenirs, in the shade of the square's centuries-old plane trees.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The tourist office and the town hall publish no rule on dogs at the market (neither permission nor ban). The market can be very busy at peak times: if you come with your dog, keep it close on a short leash and follow the signs displayed on site. Check with the tourist office (04 94 97 45 21) if in doubt.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the tourist office advises arriving at opening time, before the late-morning crowds, which is also more comfortable for a dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The port of Saint-Tropez and its cobbled lanes are a few steps from the square.</p>
    </div>

